    anyOrNumT -- THE isGROUP POISON STAYS FIXED. Minted 2026-08-29, Tony's
    ruling, the moment the fix certified and not one minute before: a POP
    captured before the fix would have pinned four refusals as truth.

    WHAT IT IS. IncantForms/WorkingOn/parser, frozen, rooted at ANYorNum, with
    every gate ON and no probe scaffolding of any kind. It walks ANYorNum and
    everything under it, generates a parse body for each, compiles each, and
    closes by parsing a specimen through ANYorNum so the run reports an answer
    rather than a count.

    WHY ANYorNum AND NOT SOMETHING BIGGER. ANYorNum is the smallest rule that
    reaches ANYtoken, and ANYtoken is the alias whose actor-without-executor
    poisoned the loader. Four rules is the whole reproduction; a larger root
    adds downstream casualties and hides which one failed first.

    WHAT WOULD GO RED, WHICH IS THE ONLY THING THAT MAKES A POP WORTH ANYTHING.
    Remove the gate on the builtinActoR attachment in Generate.rtn's setParse
    and rebuild, and this reads 4 attempted / 4 REFUSED. That was measured as
    the baseline of the three-arm probe, so the negative control is on record
    rather than asserted -- see designDocs ProblemRecords isGroupActorPoison.

    THE THREE ASSERTIONS ARE THREE, DELIBERATELY. The census line catches a
    refusal; the body target catches generation drift; the answer catches a
    parse that compiles and then does not run. One blurred check could not
    tell those apart, and they fail for different reasons.

    THE DRIVER'S STOP IS INSIDE THE ACTION, and that is the shape rather than a
    style. Binding parse methods across a grammar rewrites the grammar the
    loader is still reading, so a driver that returns to the loader is reading
    source through a grammar it has just changed. incant/parseClass carries the
    same shape for the same reason.

    ONE SENTINEL, AT THE FOOT, INSIDE THE DRIVER, reachable only through the
    verification step -- so a run that dies before reporting an answer cannot
    print it.
